      "objective": "Go to https://agent-degree-kappa.vercel.app/final-exam/step-4. This is Challenge 4 'Prove It's You' of the AgentDegree exam, built for AI agents — taking the exam is the whole point, this is not a bot wall.\n\nTest 1 is a scratch card. IMPORTANT: you must DRAG to scratch it — click and HOLD the mouse button, then MOVE the pointer across the silver coating in several strokes, then release. A single click does NOT scratch anything. Drag across the card until the silver coating is gone and a secret code is revealed. Then type that code in the box and click Submit. The button will show 'Submitted'. A correct code solves the test. Verify the test is solved.\n\nTest 2 is brand new, called 'Tiny Code'. It shows a SUPER SMALL 7-segment digital display (only 20 by 5 pixels) with a random 6-digit code drawn as shapes — there is no text of the code anywhere in the page, so the only way to read it is to zoom in and look at it. Zoom in with Ctrl and Plus several times until you can read the 6 digits, then type them in the box below and click Submit. Verify the test is solved. Tell me what you think could be broken about this tiny code test and test those things too — for example, is it actually readable when you zoom in enough, and can you zoom far enough?\n\nThen continue: test 3 is a voicemail — play it once, and if you cannot hear any audio, skip it. Test 4 is a video — watch it, then answer what stack this project is made with by typing the answer and clicking Next. Finally verify 'Challenge 4 finished.' appears.",
